From f5de1c971eb37922d58e8bd7a517ac631ba15cc5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vkd3d-crossover <noreply@vkd3d-crossover.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:02:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add DXGI call trace

Dev only, not part of release builds.

Problem: display-mode and swapchain decisions made by games through DXGI
(mode list, chosen mode, swapchain and window sizes) are invisible, which
made the 882x550 render resolution hard to explain.

Root cause: DXVK has no per-call log of the DXGI output, factory and
swapchain entry points.

Fix: rename the traced methods to *_Impl and add thin wrappers that call
them and log arguments and results: Output::GetDesc, GetDesc1,
GetDisplayModeList, GetDisplayModeList1, FindClosestMatchingMode,
FindClosestMatchingMode1; Factory::CreateSwapChain,
CreateSwapChainForHwnd (with window and client rects); SwapChain::GetDesc,
GetDesc1, ResizeBuffers, ResizeTarget, SetFullscreenState,
GetContainingOutput. Output goes to C:\gfx-dxgi.log, capped at 20000
lines.

Verified by: found the 882x550 mode selection fixed by the Windows-like
display mode list.

Off switch: off by default. Enabled by DXVK_DXGI_TRACE=1 or by the
presence of the file C:\gfx-dxgi.trace (delete it from the bottle when
done).
